~D. 1#This choice does not satisfy the required model condition. Recheck the equation or interval.
}
::PC_U01_L07_GP03::
Question ID: PC_U01_L07_GP03
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.MOD.1
Question:
Graphically, what does the solution of a system represent?
{
~A. The y-intercept of the first graph#This choice does not follow the system or interval condition. Check which equation or rule applies.
~B. The x-intercept of the second graph#This choice reflects a common mix-up with coordinates or interval boundaries. Use the given equations or inequalities directly.
=C. The point where the graphs intersect#Correct. The choice satisfies the stated system, graph interpretation, or piecewise interval condition.
~D. The interval where one graph is increasing#This choice does not satisfy the required model condition. Recheck the equation or interval.
}
